@startuml system-context
!include plantuml-style.puml
' Logical context only. No SSID, IP address or credentials.
title Wainlux K6 - system context
left to right direction

rectangle "One shared Wi-Fi network\n(SSID and addresses intentionally omitted)" as Wifi {
  node "Steam Deck\nDevelopment platform" as Deck {
    component "Rust workspace\nbuild + tests" as RustDev
    component "Ghidra analysis\nisolated container" as Ghidra
  }

  node "Pi Zero W\nLaser host" as PiZero {
    component "Rust laser service\nHTTP API + browser UI" as Laser
    component "MCP preview service\nStreamable HTTP\n(separate container, assumed here)" as MCP
  }

  node "Laptop" as Laptop {
    component "Web browser\noperator UI" as Browser
  }

  node "Pi 5" as Pi5 {
    component "neocv\nproducer/client" as NeoCV
  }

  actor "Sean Donnellan" as Sean
  actor "iPhone" as Phone
}

node "Wainlux K6" as K6 #fff/red
artifact "Bamboo card\nWi-Fi/contact QR + NFC" as Card #fff/orange

Sean --> Deck : develops; starts Ghidra analysis
Ghidra --> RustDev : protocol-only findings\n(no source/artifacts)
RustDev --> PiZero : built service image\nwhen deployed
Sean --> Browser : reviews and starts stages
Browser --> Laser : HTTP review / plan / run / verdict
MCP --> Laser : local HTTP discovery + preview only
NeoCV --> Laser : HTTP job submission / preview
Laser --> K6 : USB serial
Phone --> Card : scans QR / reads NFC
Phone --> Wifi : joins the network\nwhen QR describes Wi-Fi access

note bottom of PiZero
  Assumed context placement for MCP.
  MCP never opens the serial device.
  Rust service is sole K6 owner.
end note
note bottom of Ghidra
  Vendor binary and Ghidra artifacts stay
  inside the isolated analysis container.
  Only protocol descriptions cross roles.
end note
@enduml
